{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For the hasty one</b> is one who has no proper thought, but rather carries out his matter in haste; like it: ולבב נמהרים (and a hasty heart)."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The lemma here combines כי with והנמהר, but the syntax is compressed; I have rendered it as Ibn Ezra introducing his comment on the word נמהר."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:48.792134633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}